$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General method for synthesis of Aza-peptide
AOMKs: A solution of bromoacetyl bromide (5 eq., 0.5 M) and DIEA (5 eq.)
in DMF was added to the resin 11. After shaking overnight, the solution
was drained and the resin was washed with DMF (3x). Next, a 0.5 M
solution of 2, 6-dimethyl benzoic acid or 2, 6-dichlorobenzoic acid
(5eq.) and KF (10 eq.) in DMF were added to the resin. After shaking at
50 °C for 1h or 4h, respectively, the solution was drained, the resin was
washed with DMF and CH2Cl2, dried in vacuo, and subjected to cleavage and
purification. AcKYAhx-aD-AOMK-Cl): 14% yield. ESI-MS: 767.8 [M+H]+ 1H
NMR: (500 MHz, CD3CN/CD3OD): δ 7.47-7.41 (m, 3H), 7.01 (d, 2H, J = 8.3
Hz), 6.69 (d, 2H, J = 8.3 Hz), 4.39 (dd, 1H, J = 5.7 Hz, J = 9.2 Hz),
4.07-4.02 (m, 1H), 3.67-3.55 (m, 2H), 3.09 (t, 2H, J = 6.7 Hz), 3.04-2.99
(m, 1H), 2.89-2.74 (m, 3H), 2.24 (t, 2H, J = 7.5 Hz), 1.94 (s, 3H), 1.59
(quint, 2H, J = 7.6 Hz), 1.55-1.49 (m, 4H), 1.43-1.38 (m, 2H), 1.29-1.23
(m, 2H), 1.19-1.15 (m, 2H). HRMS: found [M+H]+ 767.2516. C34H45Cl2N6O10 +
requires 767.2574.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A General Solid Phase Method for the Preparation of Diverse Azapeptide
Probes Directed Against Cysteine Proteases
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kato, Daisuke; Verhelst, Steven H. L.; Sexton, Kelly B.; Bogyo, Matthew
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2005), 7(25), 5649-5652

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME252 STEP1
