$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General method of solid phase peptide
synthesis. Fmoc protecting groups were removed by treatment with 20%
piperidine in DMF for 15 min, followed by three washes with DMF. A 0.5 M
solution of N-Fmoc-protected amino acid (10 eq.), HOBt (10 eq.) in DMF
and sequentially DIC (10 eq.) were added to the resin. The resin was
shaken overnight. For each following step of the solid phase peptide
synthesis, the same deprotection and coupling reactions were performed,
but for each subsequent amino acid coupling, 3 equivalents of each
reagent were used. Capping of N-terminal amine was achieved by shaking
the resin with a 0.5 M solution of acetic anhydride (10 eq.) and DIEA (15
eq.) in DMF for 15 min. Removal of Alloc protecting group. The whole
procedure of Alloc deprotection was conducted under a positive flow of
argon. The resin was solvated with CH2Cl2 for 5 min. The solvent was
drained, and PhSiH3 (24 eq.) in CH2Cl2 was added to the resin followed by
Pd(pph3)4 (0.25 eq.) in CH2Cl2. After agitating the resin for 1 h by
bubbling with argon, the solution was drained, and the resin was washed
with CH2Cl2 (3x). General method for synthesis of Aza-peptide epoxides. A
0.4 M solution of ethyl L-trans-epoxysuccinic acid (10 eq.) and HOBt (10
eq.) in DMF and sequentially DIC (10 eq.) were added to the resin. After
shaking overnight, the solution was drained, the resin was washed with
DMF followed by CH2Cl2, dried in vacuo, and subjected to cleavage and
purification. AcKYAhx-aD-Michael Acceptor (13): A solution of fumaric
acid monoethyl ester (5 eq., 0.5 M), PyBOP (5 eq.) and DIEA (10 eq.) in
DMF was added to the resin 11. After shaking overnight, the solution was
drained, the resin was washed with DMF and CH2Cl2,dried in vacuo and
subjected to cleavage and purification. 13% yield. ESI-MS: 663.4 [M+H]+
1H NMR (500 MHz, CD3CN/CD3OD): δ 7.33 (d, 1H, J= 15.5 Hz), 7.06 (d, 1H, J
= 8.5 Hz), 6.79 (d, 1H, J = 15.5 Hz), 6.75 (d, 1H, J = 8.5 Hz), 4.45 (dd,
1H, J = 6.1 Hz, J = 9.7 Hz), 4.25 (q, 2H, J = 7.1 Hz), 4.15 (dd, 1H, J =
6.3 Hz, J = 7.9 Hz), 3.18-3.11 (m, 2H), 3.06 (dd, 1H, J = 6.1 Hz, J =
13.9 Hz), 2.89-2.82 (m, 3H), 2.29 (t, 2H, J = 7.4 Hz), 1.98 (s, 3H),
1.67-1.55 (m, 6H), 1.49-1.43 (m, 2H), 1.33-1.24 (m, 7H). HRMS: found
[M+H]+ 663.3378. C31H47N6O10 + requires 663.3354.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A General Solid Phase Method for the Preparation of Diverse Azapeptide
Probes Directed Against Cysteine Proteases
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
