$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The typical protocol for aminocarbonylation when optimizing the model
reaction in X-XCubeTMwas the following: 4-iodobenzoic acid (1 mmol, 0.248
g), pyrrolidine (1.5 mmol, 124µL) and triethylamine (2 mmol, 278 µL) were
dissolved in 50 tetrahydrofurane. The solution was passed through
X-CubeTM with 0.5 mL/min flow rate at 100°C and 30 bar. Carbon monoxide
gas from a cylinder was introduced to the X-CubeTM which mixed the CO gas
with the solution in its gas-liquid mixer unit. The gas-liquid mixture
then was pressed through the prefilled, preheated cartridge (CatCart®,
containing 0.4 g catalyst*) where the reaction took place. The reaction
time (as calculated from the residence time) was less than 2 minutes. The
solvent was removed under reduced pressure, resulting a product of 75%
purity and 96% conversion. Preparative HPLC chromatography (with Waters
2545-ZQ 4000 system) purification afforded the product. The reaction of
4-iodobenzoic acid (1.0 mmol, 0.248 g) and pyrrolidine (1.5 mmol, 124 μl)
was carried out as described earlier and produced 0.177 g (81%) of
4-(Pyrrolidine-1-carbonyl)-benzoic acid. Purity: 98%. 1H NMR (300 MHz,
DMSO-d6) ppm 1.54-1.68 (m, 4H), 3.32-3.38 (t, J=8.2 Hz, 4H), 8.23 (d,
J=8.2 Hz, 2H), 8.38 (d, J=8.2 Hz, 2H), 11.0 (br.s., 1H). 13C NMR (101
MHz, DMSO-d6) ppm 25.4, 47.9, 125.5, 130.9, 131.2, 141.4, 169.0, 170.3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM high pressure, solid-supported catalyst, flow system, yield depends on
reaction conditions (bsae and cat.)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM High-Efficiency Aminocarbonylation by Introducing CO to a Pressurized
Continuous Flow Reactor
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Csajagi, Csaba; Borcsek, Bernadett; Niesz, Krisztian; Kovacs, Ildiko;
Szekelyhidi, Zsolt; Bajko, Zoltan; Uerge, Laszlo; Darvas, Ferenc
