$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The typical protocol for aminocarbonylation
when optimizing the model reaction in X-XCubeTMwas the following:
4-iodobenzoic acid (1 mmol, 0.248 g), pyrrolidine (1.5 mmol, 124µL) and
triethylamine (2 mmol, 278 µL) were dissolved in 50 tetrahydrofurane. The
solution was passed through X-CubeTM with 0.5 mL/min flow rate at 100°C
and 30 bar. Carbon monoxide gas from a cylinder was introduced to the
X-CubeTM which mixed the CO gas with the solution in its gas-liquid mixer
unit. The gas-liquid mixture then was pressed through the prefilled,
preheated cartridge (CatCart®, containing 0.4 g catalyst*) where the
reaction took place. The reaction time (as calculated from the residence
time) was less than 2 minutes. The solvent was removed under reduced
pressure, resulting a product of 75% purity and 96% conversion.
Preparative HPLC chromatography (with Waters 2545-ZQ 4000 system)
purification afforded the product. 3-Iodobenzoic acid (1.0 mmol, 0.248 g)
and 1-(4-Nitro-phenyl)-piperazine (1.5 mmol, 124 μl) was carried out as
described earlier and produced 0.089 g (25%) of
3-[4-(4-Nitro-phenyl)-piperazine-1-carbonyl]-benzoic acid. Purity: 72%.
1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ ppm 3.46 (t, J= 7.1 Hz, 4H), 3.62-3.65 (t,
J=7.1 Hz, 4H), 7.11 (t, J=4.6 Hz, 2H), 7.84-7.86(m, 2H), 8.24 (m, 2H),
8.37 (m, 2H), 10.99 (br.s., 1H). 13C NMR (101 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ ppm 44.4,
49.8, 112.4, 125.5, 126.4, 130.9, 138.9, 141.4, 158.2, 168.9, 169.4.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM high pressure, solid-supported catalyst, flow system
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM High-Efficiency Aminocarbonylation by Introducing CO to a Pressurized
Continuous Flow Reactor
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Csajagi, Csaba; Borcsek, Bernadett; Niesz, Krisztian; Kovacs, Ildiko;
Szekelyhidi, Zsolt; Bajko, Zoltan; Uerge, Laszlo; Darvas, Ferenc
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2008), 10(8), 1589-1592

